WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.427
The plan sets the level. You can take over at any moment.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.591
Mid-ride, the plan holds level eighteen, and the note says levels change with each

00:00:12.591 --> 00:00:13.395
interval.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.886
Tap level twenty-two on the picker, or press plus.

00:00:21.086 --> 00:00:24.187
It reads Setting twenty-two while the bike catches up.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.045
The bike confirms it: Resistance set to twenty-two, in thirty-eight milliseconds.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.659
You're in manual now. The plan's level stays outlined, and the plan takes over at

00:00:44.659 --> 00:00:45.994
the next interval.

00:00:46.194 --> 00:00:48.478
Sent to bike logs it as manual.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.274
Or press Back to plan, and you're following the plan again.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.592
Until the bike connects, the controls wait.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.563
On a phone, the panel follows the ride totals, and the picker is one target, the

00:01:14.563 --> 00:01:15.490
full width.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.040
What the tests prove: a manual level holds until the next segment.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.110
And Back to plan sends the plan's level at once.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.515
That is journey four. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live

00:01:36.515 --> 00:01:37.825
training display.
